{
  "id": "COMPOUND:2690 - PROTEIN:6293",
  "verbalization": "Aetiocholanolone is implicated in the regulation of Dipeptidyl peptidase IX (DPPX) through a multi-step pathway involving the Liver X receptor (LXR). The evidence suggests that Aetiocholanolone acts as a target for LXR, which in turn targets various compounds, including Pregnenolone and Hydroxysaikosaponin C. These compounds, in turn, have a direct effect on DPPX. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Aetiocholanolone influences DPPX via the LXR signaling pathway, possibly through the activation of downstream targets that modulate DPPX activity. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, reinforcing the notion that Aetiocholanolone may interact with LXR to regulate DPPX, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
